The graph shows the balance owing on a reducing balance home loan.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=9.5cm,height=7cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=315,ymin=0,ymax=215000,xtick={0,50,100,150,200,250,300},ytick={0,25000,50000,75000,100000,125000,150000,175000,200000},grid=both,samples=80,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={Months},ylabel={Balance owing (\$)},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue,domain=0:300]{200000*(4.46497 - exp(x*0.0049875))/3.46497};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Use the graph to estimate how much was borrowed, and how much is still owing after $200$ months.
